On Sat, Aug 08, 2009 at 06:21:00AM -0400, Pierre Abbat wrote:
> On Friday 07 August 2009 18:28:18 Timo Paulssen wrote:
> > lojban.org is hosted on amazon cloudfront and we are currently
> > experiencing cpu steal, that's why the website is so slow -
> > sometimes so slow that it wont work at all :(
> 
> What's cloudfront? What's CPU steal?

We actually use EC2, not cloudfront; in both cases the answer is "a
hosting service".

CPU steal is when other virtualized servers are getting CPU time
such that whatever virtualized server you're looking at isn't
getting as much as it should.  If that means nothing to you, then:
I'm not getting as much CPU on lojban.org as I pay for.

